Init_Debris: contiguous Setup_Sprite info blocks (scattered-locals class)

Setup_Sprite(name, out) fills a 24-byte sprite-info block; Init_Debris keeps TWO of
them adjacent on the stack (BON88A @[ebp-0x70], BON88B @[ebp-0x58]) and reads their
UV/size fields through JOINT byte indexing: acStack_60[(car&1)*0x18 + k] selects
block A or B via the 0x18 stride. Ghidra declared local_70 as only short[6] and split
the rest into auStack_64[2]/acStack_60[8]/local_58[12]; gcc scatters separate locals,
so (a) Setup_Sprite's 24-byte write overflowed local_70 into unrelated slots and
(b) the joint-indexed reads hit stack garbage. Native and wasm compiled different
layouts -> the debris (spark) table diverged from init, and its rand()-consuming
spawn decisions desynced the shared PRNG stream at the first collision (native/wasm
state bit-diff from frame 0x97). One contiguous short[24] restores the asm frame.

